    "description": "A lion-sized 'false sabre-tooth' of Late Miocene North America, about 9 million years ago, with the longest upper canines for its skull size of any cat-like predator, sheathed by a deep bony flange on the lower jaw. Its short, massively muscled legs were made for ambush, not chases: it wrestled big prey such as rhinos and camels to the ground and killed with a slashing bite. Few animals of its time could survive its first strike."
  },
