    "description": "A giant hyaenodont of Early Miocene East Africa, about 22 million years ago, perhaps heavier than a polar bear and one of the largest meat-eating land mammals ever. It came from an old line of predators unrelated to cats, despite its name meaning 'big lion' in Swahili, and had a huge skull with long, scissor-like cheek teeth. Strong enough to tackle early elephants and rhinos, it was slow and heavy on its short legs."
  },
