    "description": "A glyptodont that walked north across the newly formed land bridge of Panama about 3 million years ago and spread into the southern United States. This car-sized armadillo relative, about 2.5 m long, was covered by a rigid domed shell of hundreds of fused bony plates, with a bony cap on its head and rings of armour on its tail. It grazed in wet grasslands and marshes, and its shell made it nearly immune to the big cats and terror birds of its day."
